// THE VOTE MODEL (12 October). Corey: "should receive vote tickets that are tradeable. you should
// be able to redeem them from your inventory if you plan to use them instead of selling them."
//
// So there are two things, and they are deliberately not the same thing:
//
//   VOTE TICKET   a stackable, tradeable obj. What voting hands out. It is an item, so it can be
//                 banked, traded, dropped and lost - and sold to another player, which is the
//                 point: a player who does not want anything in the vote shop can turn a vote into
//                 gp, and a player who does want something can buy more tickets than they voted
//                 for. The ticket is the liquid half.
//
//   VOTE POINT    a varp. What a redeemed ticket becomes, one for one. No slot, no trade, no drop,
//                 no death loss, no way back to a ticket. The bound half.
//
// WHY BOTH, rather than just making the ticket the shop's currency (which the shop system already
// supports - Grace takes Marks of Grace that way, and the TzHaar take Tokkul)? Because then every
// vote reward would be priced in a tradeable item, and the reward shop would be a gp shop with
// extra steps. The one-way redeem is what makes the choice real: tickets or rewards, not both.
//
// REDEEMING IS IRREVERSIBLE, so ~vote_redeem asks before it does a whole stack.

// One ticket, one point. Any other ratio would just be a unit change - the prices are in the same
// currency either way - so 1:1 is the ratio that needs no explaining to a player.
^vote_points_per_ticket = 1

// The stack size past which Redeem asks "one or all?" rather than silently eating the lot. One
// ticket cannot be a mistake; forty can.
^vote_redeem_ask_above = 1

// WHAT THE SHOP CHARGES. The price lives here and is written into the obj's cost= field
// (general/configs/diary_rewards.obj), because that is where the shop system reads a price from -
// ~adjusted_item_cost_buying is oc_cost($obj) scaled by the shopkeeper's per-mille multiplier.
// Grace's recolour kits are priced the same way.
//
// 50 POINTS FOR EXPLORER'S RING 4, and the arithmetic behind it: one ticket is one point, and a
// voter on a 12-hour cooldown is realistically bringing in a couple of tickets a day, so 50 is
// somewhere around three or four weeks of voting. That is meant to feel like the reward for a habit
// rather than a purchase - the ring is a full-diary item everywhere else, and the diary does not
// exist here to gate it. Change this one number to move the price; nothing else refers to 50.
^vote_price_explorers_ring = 50
